&lt;li&gt;Monitoring ETF fair value, tracking errors, and arbitrage opportunities across primary and secondary markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and maintaining reports, dashboards, and monitoring systems to track performance, risk, and operational health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing ETF lifecycle events including index rebalances, corporate actions, and dividend adjustments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with quantitative researchers to enhance and scale existing trading strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously analyzing market structure, liquidity dynamics, and venue-specific nuances to improve execution quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor&#39;s, master&#39;s, or PhD degree in a quantitative or technical discipline (e.g., Mathematics, Statistics, Computer Science, Engineering, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of hands-on experience handling Japan ETF flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of ETF mechanics, including primary/secondary market interactions, creation/redemption processes, and arbitrage dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid knowledge of index methodologies (e.g., rebalancing, constituent changes) and corporate actions (e.g., dividends, splits)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of market microstructure and regional trading nuances across APAC exchanges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work independently with a high degree of ownership and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, intellectually curious, and capable of quickly learning and adapting in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to collaborate effectively with traders, quants, and engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scripting and programming languages such as Python,&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;SQL,&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Bash&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
