&lt;li&gt;Contributing to the monitoring stack and reporting on the status and health of our systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serving as the primary technical contact for brokers and exchanges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing periodic after-hours coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have previous experience in the finance industry along with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years working in a high pressure environment, including diagnosing and resolving production issues on the fly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of electronic trading and/or financial instruments including equities, futures, and options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to manage multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment while demonstrating true ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Unix skills along with programming skills in Python and experience in Scheduling tools like Airflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Grafana&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of networking and system concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The willingness to take on tasks both big and small&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and fluency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for learning and innovative problem-solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL and the use of databases is a plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower’s headquarters are in the historic Equitable Building, right in the heart of NYC’s Financial District and our impact is global, with over a dozen offices around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, we believe work should be both challenging and enjoyable. That is why we foster a culture where smart, driven people thrive – without the egos. Our open concept workplace, casual dress code, and well-stocked kitchens reflect the value we place on a friendly, collaborative environment where everyone is respected, and great ideas win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Savings plans and other financial wellness tools available in each region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast, lunch, and snacks daily&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office wellness experiences and reimbursement for select wellness expenses (e.g., gym, personal training and more)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored sports teams and fitness events (JPM Corporate Challenge, Cycle for Survival, Wall Street Rides FAR and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities and charitable giving&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events, happy hours, treats, and celebrations throughout the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workshops and continuous learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, you’ll find a collaborative and welcoming culture, a diverse team and a workplace that values both performance and enjoyment. No unnecessary hierarchy. No ego. Just great people doing great work – together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

75ec1691c12a6a93396a733ea0880c9694534cee:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Old Mission is a global proprietary trading firm that leverages state-of-the-art technology and research to identify and execute profitable trading strategies across multiple asset classes around the world. Our offices in Chicago, New York, and London are all composed of naturally-curious individuals who thrive in a team environment and constantly strive for improvement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Head of CI/CD Engineering, you will own the strategy, architecture, and execution of our continuous integration and delivery pipelines. You&#39;ll lead the effort to build scalable, efficient, and reliable build, test, and deployment systems, leveraging Bazel as a core technology. You will collaborate with cross-functional teams to streamline our build, test, and deployment pipelines, ensuring scalability, efficiency, and reliability across our software projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the CI/CD strategy and roadmap across engineering, aligning tooling and process with business and technical goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, implement, and maintain CI/CD pipelines, using Bazel&#39;s build system as a foundation for automated testing, building, and deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, configuration, and maintenance of Bazel build rules, macros, and toolchains, and guide teams through migrations onto the platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering leadership and cross-functional teams to identify pipeline bottlenecks and drive performance, scalability, and reliability improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish best practices, standards, and documentation for CI/CD workflows, and mentor engineers on their adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve complex build and pipeline failures, acting as an escalation point for the broader team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and integrate supporting tools (containerization, artifact management, testing frameworks) into the CI/CD ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on CI/CD and build-system trends (Bazel, containerization, deployment strategies) and champion continuous improvement across the org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience designing, building, and leading CI/CD pipelines in a production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience with Bazel at scale, including build optimization and toolchain management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software development principles, release engineering, and build/deploy methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or mentoring engineers, and driving adoption of new tooling or process across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with version control systems (Git, Mercurial, etc.) and build tools (Make, CMake, Bazel)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with containerization technologies (Docker, Kubernetes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with CI/CD tooling (Jenkins, CircleCI, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong C++ or systems-level programming background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and cross-team collaboration skills; comfortable influencing without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to open-source build/CI tooling projects a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Benefits and Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid Medical, Dental, Vision, Disability, and Life Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully stocked kitchen; free breakfast and lunch every day on-site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Vacation, Sick, and Parental leaves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter and Flexible Spending Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Salary Range&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$175,000 to $225,000 - Salaries are based on numerous factors such as skills, experience, and education. Our compensation package also includes a discretionary bonus and a comprehensive benefits program for full-time employees. For more information, reach out to your recruiter.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Old Mission is not accepting unsolicited resumes from any staffing/search firms. All resumes submitted by staffing/search firms to any employee at Old Mission via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid signed search agreement will be deemed the sole property of Old Mission, and no fee will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Old Mission.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

