b382429f2199ceb06a198c1971d79caf6b116731:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a global alternative investment management firm focused on pursuing outperformance for sophisticated clients via our Systematic, Discretionary and Solutions offerings. Powered by talent and advanced technology, our single and multi-manager investment strategies are underpinned by deep research and span public and private markets, across all major asset classes, with a significant focus on alternatives. Man Group takes a partnership approach to working with clients, establishing deep connections and creating tailored solutions to meet their investment goals and those of the millions of retirees and savers they represent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in London, we manage $253.6 billion* and operate across multiple offices globally. Man Group plc is listed on the London Stock Exchange under the ticker EMG.LN and is a constituent of the FTSE 250 Index. Further information can be found at &lt;a href=&quot;https://gbr01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.man.com%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CSarah.Salta%40man.com%7C50106c0fbadc415bae6b08dd71e5d131%7Cf771e26b93bc4bbe8f6b7cd560ce9350%7C0%7C0%7C638791954087076774%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=5iuJXx8lcIhasW1cs1O9OyY6uKEhZDGiG5RgG9UVIsU%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;www.man.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-normal text-sm mb-4 last:mb-0 break-words&quot;&gt;At Man Group, we respect your privacy and we are committed to protecting and safeguarding your Personal Data. We have developed policies and processes which are designed to provide for the security and integrity of your Personal Data. We are committed to Processing your Personal Data fairly and lawfully, and being open and transparent about such Processing. For further information on how we process your data, please see the privacy notice for applicants&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;text-sm font-normal text-light-blue underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.man.com/privacy-notice-job-applicant&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* As at 30 June 2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Profile Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The primary purpose of this role is to positively position various Man products across the institutional and intermediary allocator community in China. The focus will be on relationship management through a network of financial institutions and includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All aspects of the promotion and servicing of existing allocations in the entire range of Man’s investment products and solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implementation of coverage strategy for clients and prospects in China and coordination with sales team activities for targeted clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a structured business plan, with the aim of increasing assets under management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, develop and maintain effective professional relationships with key investment contacts among the institutional and intermediary investor base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured management of designated accounts: this will involve prioritisation of accounts, research, prospecting through and introducing possible investment solutions (including bespoke solutions) provided by Man Group; involve and engage senior colleagues and senior management in these discussions where appropriate; close on opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that department operates within its regulatory obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carry out finals presentations in conjunction with Portfolio Managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage on-going relationships with new and existing clients, across the whole hierarchy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development of the overall business development strategy and help to implement the direct sales strategy achieving personal sales target within the timescales set&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other regions to ensure effective cross marketing and servicing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain contact tracking information for all key contacts so that accurate, up-to-date information is stored regarding these contacts. Ensure that all meeting notes are accurately written up in a timely manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage internal contacts to support sales activity and provide feedback on market and prospect knowledge to support and develop business strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act with integrity and diligence, observe proper standards of conduct and maintain a strong culture of compliance and ethics for all staff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the Man brand is protected and suitably publicised in the region, including responsibility for external communications including liaising with journalists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on all activity to senior management in an agreed format and within established timeframes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor, guide and manage junior members of the team, supporting their professional development and fostering a collaborative and high-performing team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role has a career trajectory, with the potential to progress to a General Manager position within the company for the right candidate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in financial markets, focused on hedge funds, fund of funds, equity strategies, trading or related fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical knowledge of investment theory and practice across asset classes, with a preference for prior alternatives experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong academics from a leading university&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently with a high level of organisation, personal initiative and resilience yet a proven ability to work well in a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influencing and distinctive communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in both English and Mandarin, both oral and written&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a pressurised and complex organisation whilst maintaining personal integrity and exhibiting good team behaviour at all times&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong networking and relationship building skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationships with Chinese distributors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chinese private fund sales experience with a proven sales track record preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In depth knowledge of Man’s products and structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people and management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organisational and time management skills to succeed in an intense, fast paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to take ownership and work independently as well as on a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven proficiency in problem resolution and demonstrated initiative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional oral and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to maintain communication and partnership with many key stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritise and multi-task&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance/Regulatory: Up to date knowledge of regulatory matters and adherence to procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion, Work-Life Balance and Benefits at Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in our working environment that champions equality of opportunity. Your unique perspective will contribute to our success, joining a workplace where inclusion is fundamental and deeply embedded in our culture and values. Through our external and internal initiatives, partnerships and programmes, you&#39;ll find opportunities to grow, develop your talents, and help foster an inclusive environment for all across our firm and industry. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.man.com/diversity&quot;&gt;www.man.com/diversity&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll have opportunities to make a difference through our charitable and global initiatives, while advancing your career through professional development, and with flexible working arrangements available too. Like all our people, you&#39;ll receive two annual &#39;Mankind&#39; days of paid leave for community volunteering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our comprehensive benefits package includes competitive holiday entitlements, pension/401k, life and long-term disability coverage, group sick pay, enhanced parental leave and long-service leave. Depending on your location, you may also enjoy additional benefits such as private medical coverage, discounted gym membership options and pet insurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants and all employees without regard to race, color, creed, national origin, ancestry, religion, disability, sex, gender identity and expression, marital status, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, age or any other legally protected category or status in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a Disability Confident Committed employer; if you require help or information on reasonable adjustments as you apply for roles with us, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:TalentAcquisition@man.com&quot;&gt;TalentAcquisition@man.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

c65f592e-4635-4845-a555-4be5838e7634:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Role &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Corporate Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation is responsible for delivering Schonfeld&#39;s highest priority strategic initiatives across our Investment, Operating, and Management Company platforms. Reporting to the Head of Corporate Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation, the Director – Corporate Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation will lead a growing team of Business Analysts and Senior Business Analysts based onsite in our 590 Madison Avenue, New York City office. You will shape the group’s vision, oversee portfolio-level planning, and ensure flawless execution of cross-functional programs that drive the firm’s long-term strategy. Our team manages a diverse range of cross-functional projects from planning to execution, connecting the firm&#39;s business strategy across the Front, Middle, and Back Office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will shape the function’s strategic direction by establishing the operating model, processes and standards that elevate business analysis, project delivery and stakeholder engagement across the firm. You will take full ownership of executing the firm’s most complex, high-impact initiatives, acting as the principal program lead for multi-project portfolios that span the entire business. A core part of your remit is to manage, mentor and develop a high-performing team of Business Analysts and Senior Business Analysts, providing continuous feedback, establishing clear career paths and fostering a culture of excellence, collaboration, and professional growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this position you will partner with executive leadership, particularly the COO and CTO to translate firm-level objectives into actionable roadmaps, OKRs, and success metrics. You will drive executive-level transparency by creating compelling analysis, steering weekly program reviews, and escalating risks with clear mitigation plans. Our ideal candidate has a proven track record in managing projects and teams within the financial services industry and demonstrates strong communication and problem-solving skills. This position is an exciting opportunity to lead transformation initiatives that directly impact Schonfeld&#39;s sustained long-term success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you need:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional leadership and people-management skills; ability to inspire, coach, and hold teams accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience leading large-scale strategic programs within financial services or management consulting, with at least 3 years managing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level project/program management capabilities: road-mapping, dependency management, risk governance, and executive reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication and influencing abilities; comfortable presenting to executive-level stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of markets, the trade lifecycle (including EMS, OMS, PMS, and trade settlement/matching), and hedge-fund operating models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;We’d love if you had: &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced data literacy; able to rapidly interrogate data, craft compelling narratives, and drive insight to action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Objectives and Key Results (OKR) frameworks across cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to continuous improvement and passion for developing talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with applying AI/ML techniques to streamline workflows and uncover strategic insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp; &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Schonfeld is a global multi-manager hedge fund that strives to deliver industry-leading risk-adjusted returns for our investors. We leverage both internal and external portfolio manager teams around the world, seeking to capitalize on inefficiencies and opportunities within the markets. We draw from decades of experience and a significant investment in proprietary technology, infrastructure and risk analytics to invest across four main strategies: Quant, Tactical, Fundamental Equity and Discretionary Macro &amp;amp; Fixed Income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Our Culture&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schonfeld, we’ll invest in you. Attracting and retaining top talent is at the heart of what we do, because we believe that exceptional outcomes begin with exceptional people. We foster a culture where talent is empowered to continually learn, innovate and pursue ambitious goals. We are teamwork-oriented, collaborative and encourage ideas—at all levels—to be shared. As an organization committed to investing in our people, we provide learning and educational offerings and opportunities to make an impact. We encourage community through internal networks, external partnerships and service initiatives that promote inclusion and purpose beyond the firm’s walls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay for this role is expected to be between $225,000.00 and $275,000.00. The expected base pay range is based on information at the time this post was generated. This role may also be eligible for other forms of compensation such as a performance bonus and a competitive benefits package. Actual compensation for the successful candidate will be determined based on a variety of factors such as skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-MM1&lt;/p&gt;

e0ea26f66df9994759bade44bddb1ea14caaf96f:
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Firm Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verition Fund Management LLC (“Verition”) is a multi-strategy, multi-manager hedge fund founded in 2008. &amp;nbsp;Verition focuses on global investment strategies including Global Credit, Global Convertible, Volatility &amp;amp; Capital Structure Arbitrage, Event-Driven Investing, Equity Long/Short &amp;amp; Capital Markets Trading, and Global Quantitative Trading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a newly created, in-house role within Verition&#39;s Tax Department supporting the personal tax affairs of the firm&#39;s principals and their related trusts, estates, and personal investment entities. Working under the direct supervision of the Global Head of Tax, this position will oversee and review the compliance and planning work performed by the firm&#39;s external accounting firms, coordinate with estate-planning counsel, trustees, appraisers, and other advisers, and serve as the day-to-day steward of the principals&#39; individual tax calendar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and manage tax compliance for high-net-worth individuals, trusts, estates, partnerships, and related entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the implementation and ongoing administration of estate, gift, and trust planning strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain books and records and prepare periodic financial statements for the principals, their trusts, and personal entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary liaison between the firm, external tax advisors, estate planning attorneys, and other professional advisors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review federal, state, and local tax returns prepared by outside accounting firms for accuracy and completeness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor tax law developments affecting high-net-worth individuals, trusts, estates, and investment structures, and assist in evaluating planning opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate annual tax projections, estimated tax payments, and cash planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support gift tax reporting, trust distributions, basis planning, residency planning, charitable giving strategies, and wealth transfer initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with entity structuring and tax considerations related to investments and private transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain tax calendars, filing deadlines, and supporting documentation across multiple entities and jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in special projects involving family office operations, succession planning, and strategic tax initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and improve internal processes and controls related to tax reporting and document management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Accounting or Taxation; Master&#39;s in Taxation preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA license strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–10 years of relevant experience in Private Client Services, High Net Worth Tax, Family Office, or a comparable practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mix of in-house and public accounting firm experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct familiarity with hedge fund / asset management flow-through pickup preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical knowledge of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Individual tax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Estate, gift and GST tax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trust and fiduciary tax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investment partnership and S-corp tax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-state tax and PTET&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technology skills including advanced Excel and a demonstrated aptitude for adopting new tools, comfortable using AI to improve the efficiency and quality of tax workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating with attorneys, trustees, and external advisors on sophisticated wealth planning matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, organizational, and project management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the discretion and professionalism required to work with senior executives and family members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of intellectual curiosity, strong work ethic, and a keen attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented, fast-paced, and dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The annual base salary range for this position is $150,000 to $200,000 (USD). In addition to base salary, this position is eligible for a discretionary performance bonus and a comprehensive benefits package. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate will be determined based on a variety of factors such as geographic location, work experience, qualifications, and skill level.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$150,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

5737532a-9b65-4efd-a12d-1269f4166b41:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Role &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the driving force behind Schonfeld’s next-generation data platforms, you will architect, operate, and continually refine underlying platform that empowers research, systematic trading, AI and risk analytics. On top of this robust foundation, you’ll build and run high-throughput pipelines spanning ultra-low-latency market-data streams to cost-efficient end-of-day workflows. Partner closely with quants, data scientists, and fellow engineers to achieve sub-minute SLAs, shape firm-wide architecture, and mentor peers. We believe diverse backgrounds and voices spark better ideas and more resilient systems, so you’ll join an inclusive culture where every perspective counts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and operate the platform – 24x7 reliability, IaC-driven deployments, tight cost controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve batch and streaming pipelines that ingest billions of market-data events each day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect high-performance, cost-efficient Lakehouse tables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expose curated datasets via robust, versioned APIs consumed by quants and AI agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize workflows to meet aggressive SLAs, embedding observability and automated data quality checks end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion Infrastructure-as-Code with Git-driven CI/CD for every data asset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior engineers and enforce best-in-class coding standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously refine processes to keep our data ecosystem resilient and lightning-fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;br&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;What you need:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years building production data platforms with Python and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in big-data architecture: partitioning, sharding, columnar formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on with SingleStore/MemSQL, Spark/Flink/EMR and event buses (Kafka/Kinesis)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven AWS skills plus Terraform / CloudFormation infrastructure-as-code mastery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering data services for AI/ML workloads and feature pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI/ML feature stores or RAG pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance-tuning Postgres, SingleStore/MemSQL, or KDB for sub-second queries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in API design, versioning, and OpenAPI/Swagger documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable collaborating directly with traders, quants, and data scientists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’d love if you had:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market-data domain expertise (tick, options, macro)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery of Iceberg, Delta Lake, or Hudi on S3&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on work with real-time analytics engines such as SingleStore/MemSQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill with performance profiling tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to open-source data tooling or technical talks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who we are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Schonfeld is a global multi-manager hedge fund that strives to deliver industry-leading risk-adjusted returns for our investors. We leverage both internal and external portfolio manager teams around the world, seeking to capitalize on inefficiencies and opportunities within the markets. We draw from decades of experience and a significant investment in proprietary technology, infrastructure and risk analytics to invest across four main strategies: Quant, Tactical, Fundamental Equity and Discretionary Macro &amp;amp; Fixed Income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Our Culture&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Schonfeld, we’ll invest in you. Attracting and retaining top talent is at the heart of what we do, because we believe that exceptional outcomes begin with exceptional people. We foster a culture where talent is empowered to continually learn, innovate and pursue ambitious goals. We are teamwork-oriented, collaborative and encourage ideas—at all levels—to be shared. As an organization committed to investing in our people, we provide learning and educational offerings and opportunities to make an impact. We encourage community through internal networks, external partnerships and service initiatives that promote inclusion and purpose beyond the firm’s walls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay for this role is expected to be between $200,000 and $220,000. The expected base pay range is based on information at the time this post was generated. This role may also be eligible for other forms of compensation such as a performance bonus and a competitive benefits package. Actual compensation for the successful candidate will be determined based on a variety of factors such as skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;#LI-TJ1&lt;/p&gt;

4d2960793a372e478430048037164b094be8bc17:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a global alternative investment management firm focused on pursuing outperformance for sophisticated clients via our Systematic, Discretionary and Solutions offerings. Powered by talent and advanced technology, our single and multi-manager investment strategies are underpinned by deep research and span public and private markets, across all major asset classes, with a significant focus on alternatives. Man Group takes a partnership approach to working with clients, establishing deep connections and creating tailored solutions to meet their investment goals and those of the millions of retirees and savers they represent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in London, we manage $253.6 billion* and operate across multiple offices globally. Man Group plc is listed on the London Stock Exchange under the ticker EMG.LN and is a constituent of the FTSE 250 Index. Further information can be found at &lt;a href=&quot;https://gbr01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.man.com%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CSarah.Salta%40man.com%7C50106c0fbadc415bae6b08dd71e5d131%7Cf771e26b93bc4bbe8f6b7cd560ce9350%7C0%7C0%7C638791954087076774%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=5iuJXx8lcIhasW1cs1O9OyY6uKEhZDGiG5RgG9UVIsU%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;www.man.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-normal text-sm mb-4 last:mb-0 break-words&quot;&gt;At Man Group, we respect your privacy and we are committed to protecting and safeguarding your Personal Data. We have developed policies and processes which are designed to provide for the security and integrity of your Personal Data. We are committed to Processing your Personal Data fairly and lawfully, and being open and transparent about such Processing. For further information on how we process your data, please see the privacy notice for applicants&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;text-sm font-normal text-light-blue underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.man.com/privacy-notice-job-applicant&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* As at 30 June 2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Algo Research Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Algo Research team is responsible for alpha research across a wide range of time-scales (from high frequency to days), design of monetisation/execution algos and market impact modelling across all major asset classes (including Cash Equities, Futures, FX, Options). We work in close collaboration with various systematic research teams across Man Group to maximise realised P&amp;amp;L of strategies. Algo Research is one of the key focus areas for Man.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Quantitative Researcher with a primary focus on Cash Equities whose responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating high quality intraday predictive alpha signals in cash equities on the scale of minutes to hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applying ML techniques to alpha research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth market impact modelling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solving optimal execution optimization problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying highest P&amp;amp;L opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close collaboration with researchers across Man Systematic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology and Business Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of work experience on the Buy side&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building intraday alpha for cash equities markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of statistics/ML and an ability to apply it to real world problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in a high-level programming language such as Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical skills; recognised by peers as an expert in their domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to conduct research independently as well as work as part of a larger team and manage multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advantageous&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of market structure, participants, trading venues and microstructure of at least one of the major asset classes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Market Impact modelling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on optimization and modelling optimal control problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with handling large data sets and tick data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Personal Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PhD or exceptional Master’s / Bachelor’s qualification in a quantitative subject&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectual integrity with a keenly analytic approach to problem solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to deliver projects with high commercial value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on attitude; willing to get involved with technology and projects across the firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-organised, with the ability to effectively manage time across multiple projects and with competing business demands and priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills, establish and maintain a close working relationship with quantitative researchers, technologists, traders and senior business people alike&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident communicator, able to challenge a point concisely and deal positively with conflicting views&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion, Work-Life Balance and Benefits at Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in our working environment that champions equality of opportunity. Your unique perspective will contribute to our success, joining a workplace where inclusion is fundamental and deeply embedded in our culture and values. Through our external and internal initiatives, partnerships and programmes, you&#39;ll find opportunities to grow, develop your talents, and help foster an inclusive environment for all across our firm and industry. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.man.com/diversity&quot;&gt;www.man.com/diversity&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll have opportunities to make a difference through our charitable and global initiatives, while advancing your career through professional development, and with flexible working arrangements available too. Like all our people, you&#39;ll receive two annual &#39;Mankind&#39; days of paid leave for community volunteering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our comprehensive benefits package includes competitive holiday entitlements, pension/401k, life and long-term disability coverage, group sick pay, enhanced parental leave and long-service leave. Depending on your location, you may also enjoy additional benefits such as private medical coverage, discounted gym membership options and pet insurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants and all employees without regard to race, color, creed, national origin, ancestry, religion, disability, sex, gender identity and expression, marital status, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, age or any other legally protected category or status in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a Disability Confident Committed employer; if you require help or information on reasonable adjustments as you apply for roles with us, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:TalentAcquisition@man.com&quot;&gt;TalentAcquisition@man.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

aeab63608629daeb4d555aa61d169307c3b8fd74:
&lt;p&gt;Tower is home to some of the world’s best systematic trading and engineering talent. We empower portfolio managers to build their teams and strategies independently while providing the economies of scale that come from a large, global organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineers thrive at Tower while developing electronic trading infrastructure at a world class level. Our engineers solve challenging problems in the realms of low-latency programming, FPGA technology, hardware acceleration and machine learning. Our ongoing investment in top engineering talent and technology ensures our platform remains unmatched in terms of functionality, scalability and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, every employee plays a role in our success. Our Business Support teams are essential to building and maintaining the platform that powers everything we do — combining market access, data, compute, and research infrastructure with risk management, compliance, and a full suite of business services. Our Business Support teams enable our trading and engineering teams to perform at their best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, employees will find a stimulating, results-oriented environment where highly intelligent and motivated colleagues inspire each other to reach their greatest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and implementing automated security solutions using Python, Bash, and related technologies to identify security exposures, optimize security infrastructure, expand capabilities, and meet business requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting and troubleshooting enterprise security infrastructure, including HashiCorp Vault, IAM, SIEM, and EDR platforms, while serving as an escalation point for security-related issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyzing security vulnerabilities and consulting on exploitation techniques, risk assessments, and remediation strategies to strengthen the organization&#39;s security posture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participating in attack simulation exercises, threat and vulnerability management initiatives, and continuous assessments to evaluate and enhance the effectiveness of security controls and incident response capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring adherence to security standards, best practices, workplace policies, and operational procedures across security engineering activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with cross-functional teams to provide hands-on support, maintain effective stakeholder communication, update senior leadership on progress, and participate in incident response activities when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s or master’s degree in computer science, information security, cybersecurity, or a related field, with at least 5 years of experience delivering enterprise security solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Unix/Linux environments, command-line administration, shell scripting, and software development using Python and Bash, along with SIEM technologies, threat hunting, security monitoring, investigations, and security documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the cyber threat intelligence lifecycle, including frameworks such as the Cyber Kill Chain and MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK, with an understanding of cyber threats in the financial sector, decentralized finance (DeFi), and blockchain technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in network and information security technologies, including IDS/IPS, NAC, DLP, VPN, firewalls, endpoint security, anti-malware, database auditing and monitoring, secure architecture design, logging, packet capture, email security, directory services, authentication, remote access, encryption, cloud security controls, and database security; experience with reverse engineering, wireless security, web application vulnerabilities (SQL injection, XSS, CSRF), exploit development, and C/C++ is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to mentor and guide security analysts, work independently with minimal supervision, collaborate across distributed teams and time zones, and effectively use collaboration and workflow tools such as Jira and Confluence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, critical thinking, problem-solving, written communication, and documentation skills, with the ability to perform under pressure, adapt to evolving security challenges, and demonstrate a self-driven approach to continuous learning and team development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower’s headquarters are in the historic Equitable Building, right in the heart of NYC’s Financial District and our impact is global, with over a dozen offices around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, we believe work should be both challenging and enjoyable. That is why we foster a culture where smart, driven people thrive – without the egos. Our open concept workplace, casual dress code, and well-stocked kitchens reflect the value we place on a friendly, collaborative environment where everyone is respected, and great ideas win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Savings plans and other financial wellness tools available in each region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast, lunch, and snacks daily&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office wellness experiences and reimbursement for select wellness expenses (e.g., gym, personal training and more)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored sports teams and fitness events (JPM Corporate Challenge, Cycle for Survival, Wall Street Rides FAR and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities and charitable giving&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events, happy hours, treats, and celebrations throughout the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workshops and continuous learning opportunities&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, you’ll find a collaborative and welcoming culture, a diverse team and a workplace that values both performance and enjoyment. No unnecessary hierarchy. No ego. Just great people doing great work – together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

6299440b-a01f-4590-9e35-a78f93ceb604:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Role&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking to hire an exceptional individual to join our Legal Team at Schonfeld. You will have the opportunity to work within two of the Legal Team’s practice areas: Portfolio Management (PM onboarding/offboarding/counseling) and Capital Development &amp;amp; Investor Relations. This is a dynamic opportunity to partner with senior management and to blend your legal acumen with your desire to get closer to the business while addressing a wide variety of legal issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your primary focus will be:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drafting, negotiating and interpreting various contracts directly with our portfolio managers (most commonly, investment management agreements, employment agreements and deeds), as well as handling related onboarding and offboarding matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All facets of fund formation and capital development, including launching new investor-facing products, updating existing fund documents, preparing and reviewing side letters, maintaining fund side letter logs, negotiating placement agent agreements, and assisting with investor queries and communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help to spearhead strategic transactions, private equity transactions, loan documents and regulatory matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering closely with our stakeholders in other departments in furtherance of the above goals, including the Firm’s CEO/CIO, COO and CFO, as well as the strategy heads, business development teams and our capital development team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working collaboratively with outside counsel and other advisers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you need:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A J.D. from an accredited law school and admittance to a state bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 4-6 years of experience in the investment management/funds practice area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house experience is preferred but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior legal analytical and drafting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior organization, communication and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and handle urgent competing workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a demanding, fast-paced and fluid environment while maintaining superior rigor and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trust and maintain positive working relationships with internal and external stakeholders at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest or experience in identifying and implementing AI tools to assist the legal team more broadly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who we are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Schonfeld is a global multi-manager hedge fund that strives to deliver industry-leading risk-adjusted returns for our investors. We leverage both internal and external portfolio manager teams around the world, seeking to capitalize on inefficiencies and opportunities within the markets. We draw from decades of experience and a significant investment in proprietary technology, infrastructure and risk analytics to invest across four main strategies: Quant, Tactical, Fundamental Equity and Discretionary Macro &amp;amp; Fixed Income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Our Culture&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schonfeld, we’ll invest in you. Attracting and retaining top talent is at the heart of what we do, because we believe that exceptional outcomes begin with exceptional people. We foster a culture where talent is empowered to continually learn, innovate and pursue ambitious goals. We are teamwork-oriented, collaborative and encourage ideas—at all levels—to be shared. As an organization committed to investing in our people, we provide learning and educational offerings and opportunities to make an impact. We encourage community through internal networks, external partnerships and service initiatives that promote inclusion and purpose beyond the firm’s walls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay for this role is expected to be between $200,000 and $250,000. The expected base pay range is based on information at the time this post was generated. This role will also be eligible for other forms of compensation, such as a substantive performance bonus and a competitive benefits package. Actual compensation for the successful candidate will be determined based on a variety of factors, such as skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;

0699d3d522f3766657de0ab3e93dc8e570288bc6:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a global alternative investment management firm focused on pursuing outperformance for sophisticated clients via our Systematic, Discretionary and Solutions offerings. Powered by talent and advanced technology, our single and multi-manager investment strategies are underpinned by deep research and span public and private markets, across all major asset classes, with a significant focus on alternatives. Man Group takes a partnership approach to working with clients, establishing deep connections and creating tailored solutions to meet their investment goals and those of the millions of retirees and savers they represent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in London, we manage $253.6 billion* and operate across multiple offices globally. Man Group plc is listed on the London Stock Exchange under the ticker EMG.LN and is a constituent of the FTSE 250 Index. Further information can be found at &lt;a href=&quot;https://gbr01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.man.com%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CSarah.Salta%40man.com%7C50106c0fbadc415bae6b08dd71e5d131%7Cf771e26b93bc4bbe8f6b7cd560ce9350%7C0%7C0%7C638791954087076774%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=5iuJXx8lcIhasW1cs1O9OyY6uKEhZDGiG5RgG9UVIsU%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;www.man.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-normal text-sm mb-4 last:mb-0 break-words&quot;&gt;At Man Group, we respect your privacy and we are committed to protecting and safeguarding your Personal Data. We have developed policies and processes which are designed to provide for the security and integrity of your Personal Data. We are committed to Processing your Personal Data fairly and lawfully, and being open and transparent about such Processing. For further information on how we process your data, please see the privacy notice for applicants&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;text-sm font-normal text-light-blue underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.man.com/privacy-notice-job-applicant&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* As at 30 June 2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Profile Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The core function of this role is to produce reports for our retail and institutional clients and work on reporting-based projects. You will have close working relationships with the Performance and Risk team as well as dealing with many other teams in the firm such as the investment teams, compliance, sales, and new product teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a 12-month fixed-term contract role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Report on a wide range of funds from Long Only, Long/Short, Credit and Managed Futures to name a few. Many of these reports are produced monthly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide an explanation of the effect of market movements on the performance of our product range and include performance, contribution/attribution, and exposure data&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Publish performance newsletters that keep the company and clients abreast of key performance movements on flagship funds and overview newsletters of content engine performance and outlooks on a weekly basis&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful individual will gain a deep understanding of the hedge fund business and develop their performance and risk skills. We&#39;re seeking someone who is capable of challenging current procedures and can accommodate the increasing demands for transparency from our institutional investors&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1-2 years of relevant industry experience, and a minimum 2:1 or equivalent in a maths or finance related degree&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Good understanding and a clear interest in financial markets&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Relevant experience/internships in a performance analyst position or similar is strongly preferred&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to manage own workload and take responsibility for tasks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective time management is essential to manage your allocation of work across the business contents&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Able to communicate effectively across all levels of the business&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Attention to detail is crucial as you will be responsible for data extraction, manipulation, validation, and control&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advanced Excel skills&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent written English&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion, Work-Life Balance and Benefits at Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in our working environment that champions equality of opportunity. Your unique perspective will contribute to our success, joining a workplace where inclusion is fundamental and deeply embedded in our culture and values. Through our external and internal initiatives, partnerships and programmes, you&#39;ll find opportunities to grow, develop your talents, and help foster an inclusive environment for all across our firm and industry. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.man.com/diversity&quot;&gt;www.man.com/diversity&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll have opportunities to make a difference through our charitable and global initiatives, while advancing your career through professional development, and with flexible working arrangements available too. Like all our people, you&#39;ll receive two annual &#39;Mankind&#39; days of paid leave for community volunteering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our comprehensive benefits package includes competitive holiday entitlements, pension/401k, life and long-term disability coverage, group sick pay, enhanced parental leave and long-service leave. Depending on your location, you may also enjoy additional benefits such as private medical coverage, discounted gym membership options and pet insurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants and all employees without regard to race, color, creed, national origin, ancestry, religion, disability, sex, gender identity and expression, marital status, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, age or any other legally protected category or status in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a Disability Confident Committed employer; if you require help or information on reasonable adjustments as you apply for roles with us, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:TalentAcquisition@man.com&quot;&gt;TalentAcquisition@man.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

52f2a24ccac44a1c4c458faaa360a7e3f322c341:
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is a leading quantitative trading firm founded in 1998. Tower has built its business on a high-performance platform and independent trading teams. We have a 25+ year track record of innovation and a reputation for discovering unique market opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower is home to some of the world’s best systematic trading and engineering talent. We empower portfolio managers to build their teams and strategies independently while providing the economies of scale that come from a large, global organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineers thrive at Tower while developing electronic trading infrastructure at a world class level. Our engineers solve challenging problems in the realms of low-latency programming, FPGA technology, hardware acceleration and machine learning. Our ongoing investment in top engineering talent and technology ensures our platform remains unmatched in terms of functionality, scalability and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, every employee plays a role in our success. Our Business Support teams are essential to building and maintaining the platform that powers everything we do — combining market access, data, compute, and research infrastructure with risk management, compliance, and a full suite of business services. Our Business Support teams enable our trading and engineering teams to perform at their best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, employees will find a stimulating, results-oriented environment where highly intelligent and motivated colleagues inspire each other to reach their greatest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Platform Engineer to help build, operate, and improve the software delivery and developer infrastructure platforms used by engineering teams working on large-scale C++ and Python applications. This role combines platform engineering, CI/CD, build systems, infrastructure automation, observability, artifact management, and developer productivity. The ideal candidate has strong systems engineering fundamentals and practical experience supporting complex engineering workflows in a production-critical environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing, building, and enhancing tools that support developer productivity, systems infrastructure, and DevOps practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the global Platform, Developer Infrastructure, and Release Engineering team to align regional solutions with global standards while representing local engineering, operational, and business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve build and release infrastructure for large-scale C++ and Python applications, including build tooling, dependency management, CI/CD integration, artifact workflows, and developer self-service capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with software engineers, infrastructure engineers, quants, traders, and SRE teams to design, build, and operate reliable software delivery platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and operate scalable CI/CD pipelines for build, test, artifact promotion, deployment, and release workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain infrastructure automation and configuration management solutions for platform, CI/CD, artifact, and developer infrastructure services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop internal developer tooling and self-service platform capabilities that reduce operational toil and improve developer productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use containerization and orchestration technologies to support reproducible builds, reliable CI/CD execution, and consistent deployment workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve observability for build, CI/CD, release, and platform services through centralized logging, metrics, tracing, dashboards, and alerting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and optimize build, CI/CD, artifact, and developer infrastructure systems with a focus on performance, reliability, scalability, and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement software supply chain security practices, including artifact provenance, dependency management, vulnerability scanning, secret management, and CI/CD security controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in incident response, root cause analysis, and continuous improvement for platform-owned build, release, CI/CD, and developer infrastructure services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and recommend improvements to build, release, CI/CD, developer infrastructure, observability, and software delivery platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of hands-on engineering experience building, operating, or improving software delivery, platform, infrastructure, CI/CD, DevOps, SRE, or developer productivity systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Linux systems knowledge and troubleshooting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software build systems, especially for large C++ codebases; experience with CMake, Ninja, Bazel, Buck2, or similar tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python packaging, dependency management, and environment management tools such as pip, conda, uv, pixi, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and operating CI/CD platforms, including pipeline design, build/test automation, artifact promotion, secrets handling, and failure diagnosis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with artifact repositories, binary/package distribution, and artifact lifecycle management using tools such as Artifactory, Nexus, Harbor, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure automation and configuration management tools such as Terraform, Ansible, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with containerization technologies such as Docker or Podman; familiarity with orchestration platforms such as Kubernetes, Nomad, ECS, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud, hybrid, or on-premises infrastructure environments; AWS, GCP, Azure, or private infrastructure experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and shell scripting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Git and collaborative development workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of networking fundamentals, including DNS, load balancing, TLS, HTTP, routing, and service discovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of distributed systems reliability concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience gathering developer feedback and translating recurring pain points into self-service tooling, automation, documentation, or platform improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to work in a fast-paced, globally distributed engineering environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Experience with:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshooting C++ build, linkage, dependency, ABI, compiler, linker, and toolchain issues in large codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modernizing legacy build systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving build reproducibility, reducing build times, or introducing remote caching / remote execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing reproducible Python environments and internal package distribution workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability platforms such as Prometheus, Grafana, OpenTelemetry, OpenSearch, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow orchestration technologies such as Airflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with GitOps deployment methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building internal developer portals, self-service workflows, or paved-road developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems programming languages such as C++ and/or Rust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software supply chain security practices such as dependency provenance, vulnerability scanning, and secret management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrating AI-assisted development tools into engineering workflows while maintaining appropriate security, access control, and code review practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anticipated New York annual base salary range $150,000 - $200,000, plus eligible for discretionary bonus.&lt;/p&gt;
