&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented, fast-paced, and dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

db0621fe411e52bc89746c2566c689d958176bd2:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Firm Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verition Fund Management LLC (“Verition”) is a multi-strategy, multi-manager hedge fund founded in 2008. &amp;nbsp;Verition focuses on global investment strategies including Global Credit, Global Convertible, Volatility &amp;amp; Capital Structure Arbitrage, Event-Driven Investing, Equity Long/Short &amp;amp; Capital Markets Trading, and Global Quantitative Trading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verition is seeking a motivated Operations Specialist to join its Middle Office Trade Support team. The Specialist will oversee day-to-day operational processes for equity and credit trading activity, including trade capture, affirmation, corporate actions, and reconciliation across multiple markets, custodians, and prime brokers. You will work closely with Trading, Portfolio Management, and other Operations teams to ensure accuracy and timely resolution of breaks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee day-to-day operational processes for equity/credit trading activity, including trade capture and affirmation across multiple markets and custodians.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply working knowledge of corporate actions processing (dividends, splits, mergers, rights issues) and help ensure timely, accurate reflection in internal systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform cash and position reconciliations between internal books/records and prime brokers; investigate and resolve breaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with trading desks and portfolio managers on trade-related matters, including settlement fails, discrepancies, and pricing issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with maintaining and improving trade flow processes, commission schedules, and related operational documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support private deal processing and DWAC/DRS flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply basic knowledge of P&amp;amp;L calculations to support ad hoc PM inquiries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support onboarding of new brokers, custodians, and counterparties from an operational readiness standpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in investment management or fund operations required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a hedge fund, asset manager, or prime brokerage preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of custodian and prime brokerage relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Excel (pivot tables, VLOOKUP/XLOOKUP; macros a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with order management/portfolio management systems (e.g., Bloomberg AIM, FLEX a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of intellectual curiosity, strong work ethic, and a keen attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented, fast-paced, and dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of private deals and DWAC/DRS transfer flow a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to derivatives, fixed income, or multi-asset operations in addition to equities a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

519c9b17c2f5713868255af5f5c138f4e33b2db7:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Firm Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verition Fund Management LLC (“Verition”) is a multi-strategy, multi-manager hedge fund founded in 2008. &amp;nbsp;Verition focuses on global investment strategies including Global Credit, Global Convertible, Volatility &amp;amp; Capital Structure Arbitrage, Event-Driven Investing, Equity Long/Short &amp;amp; Capital Markets Trading, and Global Quantitative Trading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verition is seeking a motivated Operations Specialist to join its Middle Office Trade Support team. The role provides daily Portfolio Manager support across fixed income-related trade flow and listed futures, sitting within the middle office and involving close coordination with portfolio managers, risk, product control, settlements, fund administration, technology, and operations. The ideal candidate is organized, detail-oriented, and responsive — someone who takes ownership of issues and follows through to resolution in a fast-paced, multi-PM environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and respond to Portfolio Manager requests and trade-related inquiries throughout the day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support trade capture for fixed income and listed futures strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and manage trade lifecycle events including expiries, cashflows, and corporate actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve booking discrepancies, P&amp;amp;L questions, and trade disputes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate issues to appropriate internal teams and follow through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise daily with Portfolio Managers, risk, product control, settlements, and fund admin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with technology and operations on system issues or workflow gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly with front office on open items and priority escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform daily position, cash, and trade reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve breaks between internal systems and prime broker or custodian records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support settlement fail resolution and counterparty dispute management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify operational gaps and contribute to process improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage lifecycle events for fixed income instruments including maturities, resets, and rollovers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support expiry and exercise processing for listed futures and options where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate records and ensure timely booking of all trade activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of trade support, middle office, or operations experience at a hedge fund or asset manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid working knowledge of fixed income products (bonds, rates, credit) and listed futures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of trade lifecycle events — expiries, cashflows, resets, rollovers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing daily cash, position, and trade reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills; comfortable liaising with front office and across internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized, task-oriented, and able to prioritize effectively under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of intellectual curiosity, strong work ethic, and a keen attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented, fast-paced, and dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate to advanced Excel proficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a multi-strategy or multi-PM hedge fund environment preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with OMS/PMS platforms and prime brokerage portals preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to additional asset classes — equities, equity derivatives, options, FX, or OTC products a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Economics, or a related field preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The annual base salary range for this position is $150,000 to $200,000 (USD). In addition to base salary, this position is eligible for a discretionary performance bonus and a comprehensive benefits package. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate will be determined based on a variety of factors such as geographic location, work experience, qualifications, and skill level.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$150,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

f39209790a7430aed10808a2f520634cb93fbec8:
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is a leading quantitative trading firm founded in 1998. Tower has built its business on a high-performance platform and independent trading teams. We have a 25+ year track record of innovation and a reputation for discovering unique market opportunities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tower is home to some of the world’s best systematic trading and engineering talent. We empower portfolio managers to build their teams and strategies independently while providing the economies of scale that come from a large, global organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineers thrive at Tower while developing electronic trading infrastructure at a world class level. Our engineers solve challenging problems in the realms of low-latency programming, FPGA technology, hardware acceleration and machine learning. Our ongoing investment in top engineering talent and technology ensures our platform remains unmatched in terms of functionality, scalability and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, every employee plays a role in our success. Our Business Support teams are essential to building and maintaining the platform that powers everything we do — combining market access, data, compute, and research infrastructure with risk management, compliance, and a full suite of business services. Our Business Support teams enable our trading and engineering teams to perform at their best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, employees will find a stimulating, results-oriented environment where highly intelligent and motivated colleagues inspire each other to reach their greatest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and improve internal tools, data workflows, and operational web applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop Python-based services, automation scripts, data processing jobs, and internal utilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with business users and engineers to understand requirements, clarify ambiguity, and deliver practical software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain workflows for data ingestion, transformation, validation, reconciliation, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and debug SQL queries used for reporting, investigation, and operational analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and iterate on AI-enabled internal tools for the telco team, including an internal AI chatbot/assistant for operational support, billing investigation, documentation discovery, and workflow guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop AI agent workflows and integrations with internal APIs, databases, and documentation sources using patterns such as Model Context Protocol (MCP), function/tool calling, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), and secure permission-aware access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain backend APIs and frontend interfaces for internal applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug issues across application code, databases, APIs, logs, configuration, and deployment environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve reliability, observability, test coverage, documentation, and maintainability of existing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Git-based development workflows, code reviews, CI/CD pipelines, and deployment processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate progress, assumptions, risks, and blockers clearly and early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of professional software engineering experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills, preferably in Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid SQL skills and understanding of relational databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with production or business-critical codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data workflows such as ETL, reporting, reconciliation, validation, or operational data processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with web application development, backend APIs, and frontend/backend integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in Linux/Unix environments and using Git-based workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging and problem-solving skills across code, data, configuration, and environment issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with ambiguous requirements, identify assumptions, ask targeted questions, and propose practical plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership mindset and ability to drive well-scoped tasks to completion once context and direction are clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication skills, including concise status updates and early blocker reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use AI coding tools thoughtfully while understanding, testing, and taking responsibility for the final output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications (not required)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Vue.js or similar frontend frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building internal tools, admin portals, dashboards, workflow applications, or reporting systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Docker, Kubernetes, deployment configuration, service logs, or operational troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GitLab CI/CD or similar automation systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python web frameworks such as Django, Flask, or FastAPI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with database schemas, migrations, indexes, or data validation logic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with observability tools, metrics, dashboards, alerts, or production monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in improving internal platforms, automating manual workflows, and reducing operational burden.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anticipated annual base salary range $130,000 - $170,000, plus eligible for discretionary bonus&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower’s headquarters are in the historic Equitable Building, right in the heart of NYC’s Financial District and our impact is global, with over a dozen offices around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, we believe work should be both challenging and enjoyable. That is why we foster a culture where smart, driven people thrive – without the egos. Our open concept workplace, casual dress code, and well-stocked kitchens reflect the value we place on a friendly, collaborative environment where everyone is respected, and great ideas win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our benefits include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Savings plans and other financial wellness tools available in each region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast, lunch, and snacks daily&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office wellness experiences and reimbursement for select wellness expenses (e.g., gym, personal training and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored sports teams and fitness events (JPM Corporate Challenge, Cycle for Survival, Wall Street Rides FAR and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities and charitable giving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events, happy hours, treats, and celebrations throughout the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workshops and continuous learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, you’ll find a collaborative and welcoming culture, a diverse team and a workplace that values both performance and enjoyment. No unnecessary hierarchy. No ego. Just great people doing great work – together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

