3a2281d150913497c196e16472d98da309a5d6ff:
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is a leading quantitative trading firm founded in 1998. Tower has built its business on a high-performance platform and independent trading teams. We have a 25+ year track record of innovation and a reputation for discovering unique market opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower is home to some of the world’s best systematic trading and engineering talent. We empower portfolio managers to build their teams and strategies independently while providing the economies of scale that come from a large, global organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineers thrive at Tower while developing electronic trading infrastructure at a world class level. Our engineers solve challenging problems in the realms of low-latency programming, FPGA technology, hardware acceleration and machine learning. Our ongoing investment in top engineering talent and technology ensures our platform remains unmatched in terms of functionality, scalability and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, every employee plays a role in our success. Our Business Support teams are essential to building and maintaining the platform that powers everything we do — combining market access, data, compute, and research infrastructure with risk management, compliance, and a full suite of business services. Our Business Support teams enable our trading and engineering teams to perform at their best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, employees will find a stimulating, results-oriented environment where highly intelligent and motivated colleagues inspire each other to reach their greatest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Central Execution Desk is looking for a Quantitative Researcher to build models, analytics, and decision systems that improve execution quality across global trading teams. The role sits at the intersection of market impact research, transaction cost analysis, causal inference, experiment design, optimization, and execution strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The researcher will work on understanding and improving how orders are routed, scheduled, evaluated, and optimized across brokers, algorithms, venues, markets, and trading teams. The work will combine rigorous quantitative research with practical execution-desk decision support, including market impact modeling, slippage analysis, causal inference, algo selection, broker evaluation, venue toxicity, A/B testing, and optimization under execution risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Researching market impact, execution cost, slippage, fill quality, etc. across global markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building models to explain and predict execution outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and analyzing A/B experiments to identify real execution improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working on causal inference methods&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing optimization models for various execution objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting research into centralized inventory, liquidity, risk-transfer, and crossing-style analytics to improve portfolio-level execution outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to research on execution algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building research tools, simulations, dashboards, and reports that help traders and PMs make better execution decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with traders, PMs, quant developers, and engineers to turn research prototypes into robust production analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Masters or Bachelors from a top-tier university in mathematics, statistics, computer science, financial engineering, physics, operations research, or a related quantitative field. PhD preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2–5 years of quantitative research experience, ideally in execution research, market microstructure, or financial data modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of statistics, time-series analysis, experiment design, optimization, machine learning, and financial markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large financial datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python skills for research, data analysis, modeling, and simulation. C++/Rust experience is a plus but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with convex optimization, causal inference, market impact models, stochastic control is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of market microstructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write clear research notes and explain quantitative results to traders, PMs, and engineers. Prior academic publications or comparable research writing are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anticipated annual base salary range $120,000 - $200,000, plus eligible for discretionary bonus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower’s headquarters are in the historic Equitable Building, right in the heart of NYC’s Financial District and our impact is global, with over a dozen offices around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, we believe work should be both challenging and enjoyable. That is why we foster a culture where smart, driven people thrive – without the egos. Our open concept workplace, casual dress code, and well-stocked kitchens reflect the value we place on a friendly, collaborative environment where everyone is respected, and great ideas win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Savings plans and other financial wellness tools available in each region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast, lunch, and snacks daily&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office wellness experiences and reimbursement for select wellness expenses (e.g., gym, personal training and more)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored sports teams and fitness events (JPM Corporate Challenge, Cycle for Survival, Wall Street Rides FAR and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities and charitable giving&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events, happy hours, treats, and celebrations throughout the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workshops and continuous learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, you’ll find a collaborative and welcoming culture, a diverse team and a workplace that values both performance and enjoyment. No unnecessary hierarchy. No ego. Just great people doing great work – together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

42c72361-ce57-42b9-a47c-a39b4322377a:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Acadian Asset Management is a global, systematic investment manager at the forefront of data-driven investing since 1986. Headquartered in Boston, with locations in Singapore, London, and Sydney, we manage over $232 billion on behalf of leading institutions worldwide—including pension funds, endowments, foundations, and sovereign wealth funds. We harness advanced technology, rich datasets, and multidisciplinary expertise to help clients navigate complex markets and uncover insights that may be overlooked by traditional approaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What sets Acadian apart is our people. We foster a collaborative, intellectually curious environment where ideas are tested, diverse perspectives are welcomed, and innovation thrives. We’re united by a shared purpose: delivering effective client outcomes and supporting one another in work that’s both challenging and rewarding. We offer a flexible hybrid work environment, strong benefits, and a casual but focused office culture—all designed to support the meaningful, collaborative work that defines Acadian.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Acadian is seeking an experienced and strategic Director of Tax to establish and lead the firm&#39;s tax function. Reporting to the Chief Financial Officer, this newly created leadership role will serve as the firm&#39;s senior tax advisor, responsible for developing tax strategy, overseeing corporate and fund tax matters, and partnering across the organization to support business growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Acadian expands its product offerings and wealth management capabilities, the Director of Tax will play a key role in advising on fund structures, tax-aware investment strategies, partnership taxation, executive tax planning, and cross-border tax matters. This leader will build a scalable tax organization while collaborating with Investments, Product Development, Legal, Client Service, Operations, and Finance to deliver practical, business-focused tax solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Acadian supports a hybrid work environment, with employees on-site in the Boston office three days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead Acadian&#39;s tax function, including strategy, governance, processes, and team development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the firm&#39;s senior advisor on corporate, partnership, fund, executive, and international tax matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business leaders to evaluate tax implications of new products, investment strategies, and fund structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on partnership tax planning, executive tax matters, and tax-efficient business structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee corporate, partnership, and fund tax compliance, tax accounting, and related regulatory reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic oversight of cross-border tax and transfer pricing initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor emerging tax legislation and advise leadership on business impacts and planning opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with external tax advisors, auditors, and regulatory authorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Client Service and Product teams to support tax-sensitive investment solutions and client needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable processes and internal controls that support Acadian&#39;s continued growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re Looking for Teammates With:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in accounting, Finance, or Tax; CPA required. MST, JD, or LLM in Taxation preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of progressive tax experience, including investment management, partnership taxation, and corporate tax strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Big Four or national public accounting experience strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of partnership taxation, fund taxation, executive tax planning, transfer pricing, and investment management structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on fund formation, tax structuring, and cross-border tax matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build teams, influence senior leadership, and partner across business functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding analytical, communication, and relationship management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $225,000 – $250,000 per year. Actual compensation will be determined based on a candidate’s skills, qualifications, and relevant experience. In addition to base pay, this position may be eligible for discretionary incentive compensation and includes participation in Acadian’s comprehensive benefits program, which includes health, retirement, and wellness offerings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To apply for this position or view Acadian’s open roles, please visit the Careers section of our website at:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.acadian-asset.com/careers/Job-opportunities&quot;&gt;http://www.acadian-asset.com/careers/Job-opportunities&lt;/a&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt; We will contact only selected candidates. &amp;nbsp;If you are a candidate with a disability, or are assisting a candidate with a disability, and require an accommodation to apply for one of our jobs, please email us at recruiting@acadian-asset.com.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Acadian Asset Management LLC is committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all employees and&amp;nbsp; applicants. No employee or applicant shall be discriminated against on the basis of gender, race, creed, color, sex, age, national origin, marital status, pregnancy or parenthood, veteran status, citizenship status, disability, gender identity, or sexual orientation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

22507f106df58d072927ad84baf3a1c279a92977:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Firm Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verition Fund Management LLC (“Verition”) is a multi-strategy, multi-manager hedge fund founded in 2008. &amp;nbsp;Verition focuses on global investment strategies including Global Credit, Global Convertible, Volatility &amp;amp; Capital Structure Arbitrage, Event-Driven Investing, Equity Long/Short &amp;amp; Capital Markets Trading, and Global Quantitative Trading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy coverage: Equity Long/Short.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor portfolio exposures, run stress test scenarios, and track risk metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support position and portfolio oversight — concentration, leverage, liquidity, correlation — alongside the Equity Long/Short Risk Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build working relationships with portfolio managers on day-to-day risk questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce regular and ad hoc risk reports for senior management, the investment committee, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support model validation and enhancement work in partnership with the Equity Portfolio Researcher and Central team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help ensure adherence to risk limits and internal policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–5 years of relevant risk management experience in the financial sector with a focus on equity markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Buyside experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and SQL; familiarity with AI tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with risk models and market conventions (e.g., Barra factor models).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build rapport with portfolio managers and articulate risk concepts clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of intellectual curiosity, strong work ethic, and a keen attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented, fast-paced, and dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The annual base salary range for this position is $150,000 to $200,000 (USD). In addition to base salary, this position is eligible for a discretionary performance bonus and a comprehensive benefits package. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate will be determined based on a variety of factors such as geographic location, work experience, qualifications, and skill level.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$150,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

ff5fce749db2c8760416f18ee099749150c46cd4:
&lt;p&gt;Tower is home to some of the world’s best systematic trading and engineering talent. We empower portfolio managers to build their teams and strategies independently while providing the economies of scale that come from a large, global organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineers thrive at Tower while developing electronic trading infrastructure at a world class level. Our engineers solve challenging problems in the realms of low-latency programming, FPGA technology, hardware acceleration and machine learning. Our ongoing investment in top engineering talent and technology ensures our platform remains unmatched in terms of functionality, scalability and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, every employee plays a role in our success. Our Business Support teams are essential to building and maintaining the platform that powers everything we do — combining market access, data, compute, and research infrastructure with risk management, compliance, and a full suite of business services. Our Business Support teams enable our trading and engineering teams to perform at their best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, employees will find a stimulating, results-oriented environment where highly intelligent and motivated colleagues inspire each other to reach their greatest potential.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with software developers across divisions to architect low-latency connections to financial exchanges around the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building advanced Ethernet-based communication stacks direct from chip to SFP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrating network stacks to connect to various financial exchanges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating custom logic to manage a constant inflow of data, which will need to be parsed, processed, and passed to the user space in the most efficient manner possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with software developers to develop an optimal interface between FPGA hardware and user space software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering or a related field, or equivalent professional experience, with at least 3–5 years of experience in ASIC and/or FPGA development; verification experience is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in FPGA and ASIC development using Verilog, SystemVerilog, and/or VHDL, including FPGA design flows (synthesis, place and route, and static timing analysis), Xilinx FPGA products and development tools, and industry-standard simulators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with hardware verification methodologies and tools, including cocotb, UVM, and formal verification; Ethernet protocols, PCIe, switching and routing, traffic parsing and shaping, network PHY interfacing, third-party IP/core integration, Linux environments, shell scripting, Python or similar scripting languages, and documenting design and interface specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to design and develop FPGA-based signal processing cores from system and architectural requirements, with experience collaborating across global teams and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in high-speed networking technologies, including 100 Mbps, 1 Gbps, 10 Gbps, and 40 Gbps network interfaces, and an understanding of network hardware techniques such as store-and-forward; previous experience in a high-frequency trading environment is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with FPGA kernel driver development and C/C++ programming, along with a strong mathematical foundation, analytical and problem-solving abilities, and strong communication and collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower’s headquarters are in the historic Equitable Building, right in the heart of NYC’s Financial District and our impact is global, with over a dozen offices around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, we believe work should be both challenging and enjoyable. That is why we foster a culture where smart, driven people thrive – without the egos. Our open concept workplace, casual dress code, and well-stocked kitchens reflect the value we place on a friendly, collaborative environment where everyone is respected, and great ideas win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Savings plans and other financial wellness tools available in each region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast, lunch, and snacks daily&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office wellness experiences and reimbursement for select wellness expenses (e.g., gym, personal training and more)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored sports teams and fitness events (JPM Corporate Challenge, Cycle for Survival, Wall Street Rides FAR and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities and charitable giving&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events, happy hours, treats, and celebrations throughout the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workshops and continuous learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, you’ll find a collaborative and welcoming culture, a diverse team and a workplace that values both performance and enjoyment. No unnecessary hierarchy. No ego. Just great people doing great work – together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

15ff4d95988e850d4773723cbdd8b973fa6fa3cb:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a global alternative investment management firm focused on pursuing outperformance for sophisticated clients via our Systematic, Discretionary and Solutions offerings. Powered by talent and advanced technology, our single and multi-manager investment strategies are underpinned by deep research and span public and private markets, across all major asset classes, with a significant focus on alternatives. Man Group takes a partnership approach to working with clients, establishing deep connections and creating tailored solutions to meet their investment goals and those of the millions of retirees and savers they represent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in London, we manage $253.6 billion* and operate across multiple offices globally. Man Group plc is listed on the London Stock Exchange under the ticker EMG.LN and is a constituent of the FTSE 250 Index. Further information can be found at &lt;a href=&quot;https://gbr01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.man.com%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CSarah.Salta%40man.com%7C50106c0fbadc415bae6b08dd71e5d131%7Cf771e26b93bc4bbe8f6b7cd560ce9350%7C0%7C0%7C638791954087076774%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=5iuJXx8lcIhasW1cs1O9OyY6uKEhZDGiG5RgG9UVIsU%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;www.man.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-normal text-sm mb-4 last:mb-0 break-words&quot;&gt;At Man Group, we respect your privacy and we are committed to protecting and safeguarding your Personal Data. We have developed policies and processes which are designed to provide for the security and integrity of your Personal Data. We are committed to Processing your Personal Data fairly and lawfully, and being open and transparent about such Processing. For further information on how we process your data, please see the privacy notice for applicants&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;text-sm font-normal text-light-blue underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.man.com/privacy-notice-job-applicant&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* As at 30 June 2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Profile Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To provide business facing company secretarial and administrative services within the Company Secretarial team, drawing on an awareness of internal business need and external industry trends. To build strong cross functional relationships with colleagues and to make a proactive added value contribution to corporate projects and shared goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is well-suited to a recent graduate or someone early in their career who is looking to build a career in company secretarial practice and corporate governance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To assist with the discharging of the Company Secretarial function’s responsibility for ensuring the statutory and regulatory compliance of all Man Group entities and provide a comprehensive range of company secretarial services to the UK and overseas entities as required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Listed Company Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide assistance with the preparation of the company secretarial content of the Annual Report and financial statements, including the Corporate Governance section, Board Committee reports, director&#39;s report, and notes as necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide assistance with the preparation of year-end documentation including the AGM Notice and related shareholder communications, alongside the timely discharge of regulatory filings relating to the circulation and publication of the Annual Report and AGM Notice (including ESEF obligations) as necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support on specific projects including share buyback processes, Sharesave Scheme exercises and share award grants and vestings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare, release and distribute routine Man Group RNS announcements, ensuring all internal controls are observed and regulatory deadlines met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support for the management of inside information and Share Dealing Code processes, including periodic attestations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Update the Shareholder Information and Corporate Governance content of the Man Group website with oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide input and assistance with the preparation and running of the AGM and other shareholder meetings. This may include organising of audio/visual and staging requirements, meeting materials, preparation of Q&amp;amp;As for the Board, managing the delivery of directors&#39; proxy votes, liaison with Registrars and sourcing Man staff to help run the meeting on the day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Company Secretary with plc Board meeting, Board committee and corporate governance matters as and when required, including supporting on the directors&#39; external interests schedule and maintaining the list of persons closely associated with directors (PCAs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Entity Governance and Corporate Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Update and maintain the Man Group corporate structure chart and statutory records for Group entities and respond to the business on related queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arrange overseas subsidiary minute collation and biannual review of corporate records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arrange Board approval and filing of subsidiary accounts and prepare and submit annual confirmation statements for UK subsidiaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Update and maintain subsidiary company Authorised Signatory Lists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support in the delivery of company secretarial services to Group entities, having due regard to the global regulatory requirements which apply to Man Group as a financial services and fund management Group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support and assistance on corporate transactions, corporate rationalisation or other projects. This may include, but is not limited to, board changes, capital injections or reductions, distributions, intercompany or external transactions and advice on any related Group governance and company secretarial practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Development and Other Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the preparation and monitoring of the annual departmental budget, with guidance from the Company Secretary, and help track expenditure against budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the team&#39;s AI enhancement initiatives and contribute to data collection and integration processes, to help deliver improved analytical insight and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Answer company secretarial queries from the business as required including queries sent to the Company Secretarial inbox.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for the team&#39;s hard copy and electronic filing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Company Secretary to raise the profile of the Company Secretarial team across the business through proactive value-added contribution to corporate projects and the development of strong relationships with colleagues in other functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide team members with any additional support they may need on ad hoc projects or their ongoing responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to draft clear, accurate documents and correspondence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and a methodical approach to work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good organisational and time management skills, with the ability to prioritise and manage multiple tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office suite (Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in and demonstrable enthusiasm for company secretarial practice - candidates should be prepared to articulate why they are looking to pursue a career in this field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative team player with a proactive attitude and willingness to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of, or interest in, using AI or data tools to improve process efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion, Work-Life Balance and Benefits at Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in our working environment that champions equality of opportunity. Your unique perspective will contribute to our success, joining a workplace where inclusion is fundamental and deeply embedded in our culture and values. Through our external and internal initiatives, partnerships and programmes, you&#39;ll find opportunities to grow, develop your talents, and help foster an inclusive environment for all across our firm and industry. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.man.com/diversity&quot;&gt;www.man.com/diversity&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll have opportunities to make a difference through our charitable and global initiatives, while advancing your career through professional development, and with flexible working arrangements available too. Like all our people, you&#39;ll receive two annual &#39;Mankind&#39; days of paid leave for community volunteering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our comprehensive benefits package includes competitive holiday entitlements, pension/401k, life and long-term disability coverage, group sick pay, enhanced parental leave and long-service leave. Depending on your location, you may also enjoy additional benefits such as private medical coverage, discounted gym membership options and pet insurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants and all employees without regard to race, color, creed, national origin, ancestry, religion, disability, sex, gender identity and expression, marital status, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, age or any other legally protected category or status in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a Disability Confident Committed employer; if you require help or information on reasonable adjustments as you apply for roles with us, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:TalentAcquisition@man.com&quot;&gt;TalentAcquisition@man.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

8a1de2e58d1a797ed489c3bf63d38ddf6fed348c:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a global alternative investment management firm focused on pursuing outperformance for sophisticated clients via our Systematic, Discretionary and Solutions offerings. Powered by talent and advanced technology, our single and multi-manager investment strategies are underpinned by deep research and span public and private markets, across all major asset classes, with a significant focus on alternatives. Man Group takes a partnership approach to working with clients, establishing deep connections and creating tailored solutions to meet their investment goals and those of the millions of retirees and savers they represent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in London, we manage $253.6 billion* and operate across multiple offices globally. Man Group plc is listed on the London Stock Exchange under the ticker EMG.LN and is a constituent of the FTSE 250 Index. Further information can be found at &lt;a href=&quot;https://gbr01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.man.com%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CSarah.Salta%40man.com%7C50106c0fbadc415bae6b08dd71e5d131%7Cf771e26b93bc4bbe8f6b7cd560ce9350%7C0%7C0%7C638791954087076774%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=5iuJXx8lcIhasW1cs1O9OyY6uKEhZDGiG5RgG9UVIsU%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;www.man.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-normal text-sm mb-4 last:mb-0 break-words&quot;&gt;At Man Group, we respect your privacy and we are committed to protecting and safeguarding your Personal Data. We have developed policies and processes which are designed to provide for the security and integrity of your Personal Data. We are committed to Processing your Personal Data fairly and lawfully, and being open and transparent about such Processing. For further information on how we process your data, please see the privacy notice for applicants&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;text-sm font-normal text-light-blue underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.man.com/privacy-notice-job-applicant&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* As at 30 June 2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance Business Partnering (FBP) team sits at the heart of Finance, working directly with senior business unit leaders, ExCo, and the Board to deliver high-quality financial insight, reporting, and challenge. The team plays a critical role in driving informed decision-making across the firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Manager within the FBP team, you will take ownership of a portfolio of Business Units, acting as a trusted financial adviser to senior stakeholders. This is a high-visibility role offering genuine exposure to the firm&#39;s leadership and the opportunity to shape how finance supports and influences the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering and developing strong relationships with key senior stakeholders within assigned Business Units and across Finance, including direct engagement with ExCo-level business leaders to provide financial insight and challenge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering monthly Direct Contribution reporting to Investment Management teams, covering revenue, AUM, margins, seed capital and associated costs, providing insight and commentary to support performance oversight and decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading monthly meetings with business managers to review financials, provide positive challenge and understand the BU’s operations and cost drivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing timely, relevant and informative management information and analysis to assigned BUs, including commentary and variance analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading the budgeting and forecasting processes for assigned Business Units, coordinating inputs from business managers, challenging assumptions, and delivering consolidated outputs to the CFO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving the month end close process ensuring the timely delivery of accurate management information on a consolidated and BU level, including monthly cost accrual postings and ledger review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting monthly cost analysis and commentary provided to the Group Reporting Team and CFO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the year-end close process, including liaison with the Group Reporting and external audit teams to provide relevant management accounts analysis and commentary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing ad hoc analysis for the business as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving strategic and operational improvements across the FBP function, including leading initiatives to enhance management information quality, automate reporting processes, leverage AI tools, and develop finance systems and tooling including Power BI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing and developing direct reports, including setting clear objectives, conducting performance reviews, supporting career development, managing day-to-day workload prioritisation, and contributing to recruitment and onboarding as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide cover and support to the Head of Finance Business Partnering as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your background / experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified in a relevant accounting qualification (ACA/ACCA/CIMA or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 2–3 years post-qualification experience (PQE) in a finance business partnering or FP&amp;amp;A role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in asset management or financial services strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Power BI experience beneficial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop trusted relationships at all levels with business and finance stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, verbal and written communication skills essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel skills, with desire and ability to learn new systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ERP or financial planning systems (e.g. Oracle, SAP, Workday Adaptive)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion, Work-Life Balance and Benefits at Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in our working environment that champions equality of opportunity. Your unique perspective will contribute to our success, joining a workplace where inclusion is fundamental and deeply embedded in our culture and values. Through our external and internal initiatives, partnerships and programmes, you&#39;ll find opportunities to grow, develop your talents, and help foster an inclusive environment for all across our firm and industry. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.man.com/diversity&quot;&gt;www.man.com/diversity&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll have opportunities to make a difference through our charitable and global initiatives, while advancing your career through professional development, and with flexible working arrangements available too. Like all our people, you&#39;ll receive two annual &#39;Mankind&#39; days of paid leave for community volunteering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our comprehensive benefits package includes competitive holiday entitlements, pension/401k, life and long-term disability coverage, group sick pay, enhanced parental leave and long-service leave. Depending on your location, you may also enjoy additional benefits such as private medical coverage, discounted gym membership options and pet insurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants and all employees without regard to race, color, creed, national origin, ancestry, religion, disability, sex, gender identity and expression, marital status, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, age or any other legally protected category or status in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a Disability Confident Committed employer; if you require help or information on reasonable adjustments as you apply for roles with us, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:TalentAcquisition@man.com&quot;&gt;TalentAcquisition@man.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

1800cf931568bbf7823606af6fa6eb581634768a:
&lt;p&gt;Tower is home to some of the world’s best systematic trading and engineering talent. We empower portfolio managers to build their teams and strategies independently while providing the economies of scale that come from a large, global organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineers thrive at Tower while developing electronic trading infrastructure at a world class level. Our engineers solve challenging problems in the realms of low-latency programming, FPGA technology, hardware acceleration and machine learning. Our ongoing investment in top engineering talent and technology ensures our platform remains unmatched in terms of functionality, scalability and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, every employee plays a role in our success. Our Business Support teams are essential to building and maintaining the platform that powers everything we do — combining market access, data, compute, and research infrastructure with risk management, compliance, and a full suite of business services. Our Business Support teams enable our trading and engineering teams to perform at their best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, employees will find a stimulating, results-oriented environment where highly intelligent and motivated colleagues inspire each other to reach their greatest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing, building, maintaining and operating bare metal Kubernetes clusters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing Kubernetes operator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning, maintaining, developing tooling and documentation for developers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Packaging, maintaining platform as a service build blocks such as stream services, data orchestrators, databases, caches, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bringing innovation to the Platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A master’s degree or PhD in computer science or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3–7 years of experience working with Kubernetes as both a user and administrator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in one or more programming languages, including Python, Rust, Go, or C++, with strong knowledge of system programming, Linux, and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure as code, large-scale configuration management systems, observability practices and tooling, and distributed systems such as Kafka and Etcd.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of infrastructure technologies and protocols, including DNS, networking, security, enterprise storage solutions, and GPU operations and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to troubleshoot complex systems and collaborate effectively in large-scale infrastructure environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower’s headquarters are in the historic Equitable Building, right in the heart of NYC’s Financial District and our impact is global, with over a dozen offices around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, we believe work should be both challenging and enjoyable. That is why we foster a culture where smart, driven people thrive – without the egos. Our open concept workplace, casual dress code, and well-stocked kitchens reflect the value we place on a friendly, collaborative environment where everyone is respected, and great ideas win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Savings plans and other financial wellness tools available in each region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast, lunch, and snacks daily&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office wellness experiences and reimbursement for select wellness expenses (e.g., gym, personal training and more)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored sports teams and fitness events (JPM Corporate Challenge, Cycle for Survival, Wall Street Rides FAR and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities and charitable giving&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events, happy hours, treats, and celebrations throughout the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workshops and continuous learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, you’ll find a collaborative and welcoming culture, a diverse team and a workplace that values both performance and enjoyment. No unnecessary hierarchy. No ego. Just great people doing great work – together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

f0dd738e-2186-4030-9793-ab73281981ef:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Role&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a qualified Executive Assistant to support a small team of Portfolio Managers at Schonfeld in Singapore. The ideal candidate is self-motivated, professional, and capable of managing a diverse workload and prioritizing tasks in a fast-paced corporate environment.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role with many hats; this candidate will be responsible for extensive scheduling and calendar management, preparing agendas for meetings, expenses, answering phones and taking messages. They will arrange domestic and international travel, accommodations, itineraries, and all correspondence related to arrangements including flights, hotels, car service, meetings, restaurant reservations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you need:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written &amp;amp; verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Microsoft Outlook and Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Powerpoint)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and manage multiple streams of information &amp;amp; tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process-oriented and very strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Efficient time management and strong sense of urgency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional organizational and time-management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-Starter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personable, mature, and poised&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team player&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’d love if you had:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Navan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with organizing events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who we are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Schonfeld is a global multi-manager hedge fund that strives to deliver industry-leading risk-adjusted returns for our investors. We leverage both internal and external portfolio manager teams around the world, seeking to capitalize on inefficiencies and opportunities within the markets. We draw from decades of experience and a significant investment in proprietary technology, infrastructure and risk analytics to invest across four main strategies: Quant, Tactical, Fundamental Equity and Discretionary Macro &amp;amp; Fixed Income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Our Culture&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Schonfeld, we’ll invest in you. Attracting and retaining top talent is at the heart of what we do, because we believe that exceptional outcomes begin with exceptional people. We foster a culture where talent is empowered to continually learn, innovate and pursue ambitious goals. We are teamwork-oriented, collaborative and encourage ideas—at all levels—to be shared. As an organization committed to investing in our people, we provide learning and educational offerings and opportunities to make an impact. We encourage community through internal networks, external partnerships and service initiatives that promote inclusion and purpose beyond the firm’s walls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

5be6c05a-9bb1-4b68-9f1a-88fa96ad9cfd:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Role&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly qualified and talented Quantitative Strategist to support the Volatility and Emerging-markets + delta-1 trading teams. You will work as part of a centralized Strategist team, working on vanilla and exotic product modelling, parameter marking and risk representation across geographies and markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategist, you will support portfolio managers trading derivatives in representing, rationalizing and understanding risk at a product and book level– ensuring that risk is accurate and economically consistent with product/payoff definitions. In addition, there will be focus on creating and understanding stressed market scenarios and developing modelling to predict product + book behavior in those environments. You will support portfolio managers and traders maintaining and extending a centralized library for valuation and risk calculations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;br&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;What you need:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with equity derivatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background and intuition in financial mathematics, adopting a first-principles approach to understanding product behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with quantitative risk teams, traders, and portfolio managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership experience and a track record of delivering results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who we are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Schonfeld Strategic Advisors is a global multi-strategy, multi-manager investment platform that harnesses the transformative power of people to perform in all market environments. Our dynamic culture inspires better outcomes for our team, our investors, and our partners. We aim to consistently deliver risk-adjusted returns, with people driving performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We specialize in four core strategies: Quantitative Trading, Fundamental Equity, Tactical Trading, and Discretionary Macro &amp;amp; Fixed Income. We capitalize on inefficiencies and opportunities within the markets, drawing from a significant investment in proprietary technology, infrastructure, and risk analytics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest through internal portfolio managers and external partner funds, pursuing alignment among investors, investment professionals, and the firm. Our footprint spans 7 countries and 19 offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Our Culture&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Talent is our strategy. We believe our success is because of our people, so putting our talent above all else is our top priority. We are teamwork-oriented, collaborative, and encourage ideas—at all levels—to be shared. As an organization committed to investing in our people, we provide learning &amp;amp; educational offerings and opportunities to make an impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We foster a sense of belonging among all of our employees with Diversity, Equity and Inclusion at the forefront of this mission. Our employees value diversity across identity, thought, people and perspective which serves as the foundation of our culture. As a firm, we are committed to creating a hiring process that is fair, welcoming and supportive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-LC1&lt;/p&gt;

375147132dc3c87a6578470a1ffd9368aa7a5f88:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Old Mission is a global proprietary trading firm that leverages state-of-the-art technology and research to identify and execute profitable trading strategies across multiple asset classes around the world. Our offices in Chicago, New York, and London are all composed of naturally-curious individuals who thrive in a team environment and constantly strive for improvement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Old Mission, a global trading firm, is looking for a Co-Op student to join our Compliance Team in Chicago, IL (15–25 hours/week, flexible). You&#39;ll work as a compliance generalist, supporting surveillance, research, and administrative work across the Firm&#39;s compliance program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond day-to-day tasks and project work, you&#39;ll get direct mentorship from senior Compliance team members and exposure to our Operations and Risk teams giving you a real, ground-level view of how compliance functions inside a large trading firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a term-renewable position with potential for full-time hire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research new trading initiatives to help the Compliance Team map out a compliant path forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with external databases including FINRA&#39;s Central Registration Depository (CRD) and My Compliance Office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support daily surveillance reviews of the Firm&#39;s options, futures, and equity trading activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help manage critical daily functions like CAT (Consolidated Audit Trail) reporting and exchange symbol registrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in reviewing existing compliance practices against regulatory requirements and industry best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rising senior based in Chicago, studying business, finance, economics, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interested in a long-term career in Compliance, Risk, or Operations at a trading firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to balance coursework with work obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some familiarity with large data sets and programming languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of exchange/OTC trading and market making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized with strong attention to detail, comfortable in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works well both independently and on a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with Microsoft Office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completed the SIE (Securities Industry Essentials) exam&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior internship experience in the industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python or SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Range&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$30/hr. ($62,400 annually based on a 40-hour work week). Compensation is determined based on experience, skills, and qualifications relative to role requirements. This position is classified as non-exempt and is eligible for overtime pay in accordance with the Fair Labor Standards Act and Illinois state wage and hour law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Old Mission is not accepting unsolicited resumes from any staffing/search firms. All resumes submitted by staffing/search firms to any employee at Old Mission via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid signed search agreement will be deemed the sole property of Old Mission, and no fee will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Old Mission.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

f127068f2480e4953972626be9fd4917d1029da1:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Firm Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verition Fund Management LLC (“Verition”) is a multi-strategy, multi-manager hedge fund founded in 2008. &amp;nbsp;Verition focuses on global investment strategies including Global Credit, Global Convertible, Volatility &amp;amp; Capital Structure Arbitrage, Event-Driven Investing, Equity Long/Short &amp;amp; Capital Markets Trading, and Global Quantitative Trading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process and review invoices across domestic and international entities, ensuring proper GL coding, cost allocations, and approval workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor onboarding, documentation, and ongoing vendor relationships, ensuring compliance with firm policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer the U.S. employee expense reimbursement process through Concur, ensuring compliance with the firm&#39;s Travel &amp;amp; Expense Policy while supporting the continued expansion of the global T&amp;amp;E program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to vendor and internal inquiries, independently resolving payment discrepancies and other AP-related issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review monthly expense allocations, ensuring costs are accurately distributed across entities, departments, and cost centers in accordance with firm methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform analytical reviews of vendor spend and expense classifications, identifying coding inconsistencies and partnering with Corporate Accounting and FP&amp;amp;A to ensure accurate financial reporting and Budget-to-Actual reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own intercompany reporting and reconciliations across all entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide cash reporting and month-end close support in coordination with the AP Manager and Controller.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and maintain analytical schedules supporting month-end close, Budget-to-Actual reporting, and management reporting for both U.S. and international entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage quarterly Sales &amp;amp; Use Tax (SUT) review and filing support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain AP documentation standards and support internal and external audit requests, ensuring compliance with firm policies and internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support AP onboarding for new domestic and international entities as the firm&#39;s global footprint continues to expand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, recommend, and drive process improvements and automation initiatives across the global Accounts Payable function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–7 years of Accounts Payable or corporate accounting experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hedge fund, alternative investment, asset management, or financial services experience strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a multi-entity, global accounting environment with intercompany transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Sales &amp;amp; Use Tax concepts and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP and Accounts Payable platforms; proficiency with StavPay is strongly preferred. Concur experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Microsoft Excel skills, including the ability to analyze and reconcile large datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate across Accounting, FP&amp;amp;A, Operations, and international teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of intellectual curiosity, strong work ethic, and a keen attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented, fast-paced, and dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

a038618afa73cb011ac75a60c7f1a72f26266207:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The HR Manager will be located in our Hong Kong or Singapore office and support India, Singapore, Dubai, Hong Kong, China and Australia. The role will work closely with the APAC HR team, senior leadership in these offices and will be part of the global HR team.&amp;nbsp; This role will report to the Head of HR APAC. The HR Manager is responsible for acting as an advisor to leaders and staff, will be an advocate for employees and will help execute global projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead all people matters in regions and ensure all HR operations align with the firm’s requirements and local legal requirements in the different countries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively address employee relations issues with leaders and provide coaching on how to handle, ensuring consistency in approach and mitigating risk for the firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and support the payroll process for regions, working closely with the global payroll team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeping up to date with local legislative changes and updating contracts and policies where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage tools to provide metrics and reporting that will help drive people decisions such as engagement metrics and turnover metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with global HR team members across regions (Payroll, L&amp;amp;D, Benefits, HRIS) to roll out key HR transformation projects such as new process and system implementations, policies/procedures and the related automation when applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure company’s procedures comply with employment regulations in the supported countries and implement the appropriate ones when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure employee issues and concerns are responded to in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee onboarding and off boarding activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor immigration matters, partnering with our third-party immigration law firm to include applying for visas, and tracking the status and all activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a team of one or two HR Specialist ensuring continuous learning and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of eight (8) years of HR experience; preferably in financial services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous exposure to employment law in India, Singapore and Hong Kong &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical reasoning and solution-focused problem solver with the ability to think critically and independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive to results, in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong prioritization and time management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovative in approaching situations and responsible to be an advocate for change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capable of synthesizing information concisely and easily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated and disciplined individual with analytical skills; capability to work independently as well as in teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills with ability to effectively interact with all levels within the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasional travelling is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works well under pressure; flexible work style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Microsoft Excel, Word, Access and PowerPoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Workday and Greenhouse (ideal but not required).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

8a4255be6ef9e5b42b9e29277a7b6a64200106bd:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This internship is based in London and is available throughout the year. Please indicate your preferred start month in the application questions.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The minimum length of the Internship must be&amp;nbsp;12 weeks.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Squarepoint&amp;nbsp;sits at the intersection of finance, mathematics, and technology. From petabyte-scale data platforms to ultra-low-latency trading systems, we build the infrastructure that powers systematic investing across every major asset class and market worldwide.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for highly motivated students with a deep passion for technology and software development to join our&amp;nbsp;Software&amp;nbsp;Developer&amp;nbsp;Internship program. As a participant in the internship program, you will work closely with experienced engineers to develop and deliver custom software solutions that solve complex problems.&amp;nbsp;During your time with us,&amp;nbsp;you will work in collaboration with your mentors on&amp;nbsp;a project that has a visible impact&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;the business.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have internship opportunities across various teams&amp;nbsp;including;&amp;nbsp;Data Engineering, Risk, Market Data, Quant Development, Frontend and&amp;nbsp;many more...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A fast-paced training program to give you an introduction to all technical&amp;nbsp;facets&amp;nbsp;of software development in the algorithmic trading industry&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The software you build and the projects you work on will be&amp;nbsp;leveraged&amp;nbsp;to support active and ongoing trading with the markets  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independent programming projects in Python or C++&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intern social events to let you network with other&amp;nbsp;Squarepoint&amp;nbsp;employees and explore the city where&amp;nbsp;you’re&amp;nbsp;spending your internship&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pursuing a degree in Computer Science, Computer/Electrical Engineering,&amp;nbsp;Mathematics&amp;nbsp;or equivalent&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates must be in penultimate year of study&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of one or more of the following programming languages: Python, C++, Java, Rust, C&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Unix systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep passion for technology&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional problem-solving skills&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;strong communication&amp;nbsp;skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

a4efc5d0-a827-41cb-801e-b326ac328750:
&lt;p&gt;Quantbot Technologies is a leading global quantitative investment firm deploying systematic strategies across asset classes. At the heart of our approach is large-scale research powered by advanced computing infrastructure and petabytes of comprehensive market and historical data. We combine rigorous scientific methods with modern statistical and machine learning techniques to discover, test, and implement novel investment ideas.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Data Trading Analyst Intern, you’ll have the opportunity to work with Quantbot’s Data Trading Lab team, a technical group specializing in trading operations, data science, and problem-solving. You will evaluate new datasets, and utilize our advanced cloud environment to write and maintain Python scripts. You will work directly with the Hong Kong team to process and assess new datasets and take part in developing new tools and infrastructure at Quantbot.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct exploratory data analysis on alternative datasets to explore datasets for potentially predictive signals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform statistical analysis including correlation studies, regression analysis, and time-series modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build ETL processes to integrate new data sources with existing research infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop data quality monitoring tools to detect anomalies and ensure dataset integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize existing scripts for performance and scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build internal Python libraries or tools to standardize common analytical workflows across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enrollment in a Bachelor’s, Master’s, or PhD program in Computer Science or Data Science related field. Seniors and students in their penultimate year are encouraged to apply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Linux or UNIX environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of SQL queries and any relational database systems is preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finance knowledge is beneficial but not essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;This 10 to 12-week program runs from June to August, offering training and support with a dedicated mentor. Successful interns may receive full-time job offers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Join a global team that values a relaxed, collaborative environment. Enjoy company outings, traditional Friday lunches, and a focus on work-life balance. Quantbot is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where all employees can thrive. Join us for a dynamic opportunity to grow with a pioneering quant firm and acquire skills for your future career.&lt;/p&gt;

